sequenceDiagram
    actor U as Marketing Team User
    participant FE as PostsList<br/>«view»
    participant RC as ReportController<br/>«controller»
    participant RS as ReportService<br/>«service»
    participant ReR as ReviewRepository<br/>«repository»
    participant PR as PostRepository<br/>«repository»

    U->>FE: open /reports/{reportId}/posts (filters in URL)
    FE->>RC: GET /api/reports/{reportId}/posts?relevance,sentiment,emotion,aspect,language,dates,page
    Note over FE,RC: all query params are optional —<br/>relevance defaults to RELEVANT
    RC->>RS: listPosts(reportId, filters, pageable)
    Note over RS,PR: two paths: relevant posts JOIN review (sentiment/emotion/aspect),<br/>irrelevant posts have no review row —> different data shapes & filter sets
    alt relevance = RELEVANT
        RS->>ReR: findRelevantPostsForReport(reportId, filters)
        ReR-->>RS: page of post + review
    else relevance = IRRELEVANT
        RS->>PR: findPostsWithFilters(reportId, filters)
        PR-->>RS: page of post
    end
    RS-->>RC: page of PostListItemResponse
    RC-->>FE: 200 OK
    FE-->>U: paginated table + post detail modal

    opt export current filter to CSV
        U->>FE: click "Export CSV"
        FE->>RC: GET /api/reports/{reportId}/export?{same filters}
        RC->>ReR: re-run review query (no pagination)
        ReR-->>RC: all matching rows
        RC->>RC: build CSV in memory (ByteArrayOutputStream)
        RC-->>FE: text/csv with Content-Disposition (filename=report-{id}.csv)
        FE-->>U: browser saves report-{id}.csv
    end
